    "summaryDescription": "This poster is free of text, with only the subtle logo of the London Underground visible in the bottom left corner. A wonderful example of the poster acting as an example of art in the streets, its message is simple: visit woodland by public transport. Its painterly style is in the school of British Modernist landscapes of the earlier 20th century. A second poster was also designed (E.715A-1950) which includes a vignette of poetic text praising the joys of a walk in the countryside.",
